1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Updating Landfall
Uninstall the old version first, then install the new one

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.883
Installing a new zip over an old one is not reliable: Blender can keep running the old code while showing the new number.

3
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:14.317
So: Preferences › Get Extensions, search for landfall.

4
00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:19.750
From the arrow next to the extension choose Uninstall. Theme, grid and navigation go back to Blender's own by themselves.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.183
Close Blender and open it again: no compiled copy of the old code stays in memory that way.

6
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:30.617
Then Preferences › Add-ons › Install from Disk… with the new zip, as at the first installation.

7
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:36.050
Check the version number in the preferences: it must be the one of the zip. The Maya set-up comes back on by itself.

8
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:41.483
Setup › Self check verifies menus, shortcuts and keymaps; two NOTEs about Alt+Q and Alt+W are normal.

9
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:44.917
Done
What changed in each version is in the CHANGELOG

